   "draft": {
    "headline": "Jake White's first Fiji game is a rematch of the final",
    "beats": [
     "Jake White, 62, was named Fiji coach on 13 October from 31 applicants. His first game is against Japan, on the ground where they beat Fiji 20–15 in the Pacific Nations Cup final five weeks ago.",
     "The previous final went the other way, 33–27 to Fiji in Salt Lake City in 2025. In September, Eddie Jones's Japan took the title back, their first since 2019.",
     "Japan have won three straight, including 63–14 against the USA and 57–12 against Canada. Fiji have won once this year. White wants Fiji to play like Fiji, with \"a little bit more structure, a little bit more formation\".",
     "A Fiji win lifts them to 9th, above Japan, and drops Japan below Wales and Italy, 12th at best. A defeat sends Fiji there instead.",
     "A fortnight later both are in Europe, Japan at Wales and Fiji at France."
    ],
    "sources": 3
